      "math_academy_id": "q-159352",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y,$ for $(x,y)\\in [0,1]\\times [0,1],$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)={2}^{xy}-1.\n$$\n\nFind ${F}_{X}(x),$ the marginal CDF of $X,$ for $0\\le x\\le 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The marginal CDF of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=F(x,\\infty )={lim}_{y\\to \\infty }F(x,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $0\\le x\\le 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{X}(x) & =F(x,\\infty ) \\\\  & =F(x,1) \\\\  & ={2}^{x(1)}-1 \\\\  & ={2}^{x}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
